Package: xo-ansible-inventory-manager
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, python3 (>= 3.9), python3-yaml
Recommends: ansible-core | ansible
Description: Dynamic Ansible inventory built from a folder of YAML files
 An Ansible inventory script that builds the inventory from a tree of YAML
 files: one file (or folder) per host, one file (or folder) per group, and
 shared variable files.
 .
 Features:
  - Groups defined by files or nested folders, with child groups
  - host_criteria expressions that add hosts to groups automatically
    (e.g. "app = proxmox AND cores >= 16")
  - enabled: false to switch hosts or groups off without deleting them
  - Optional cache that is invalidated whenever the inventory changes
 .
 Configure /etc/ansible/xo_inventory.yaml, then point Ansible at
 /usr/bin/ansible-xo-inventory.py.
